{"kind":"request","text":"Attack-surface reduction of dap: findings at main 603220b9 and the remediation to file\n\nRead-only review of main 603220b9 on 2026-10-21, using the three lenses of Anthropic's \"attack surface reduction\" method (https://www.anthropic.com/research/attack-surface-reduction): default configuration, early reachability, configuration interaction. Three parallel code inventories (scope Worker; hosted MCP endpoint with host ports and application packages; configuration interactions) plus line-by-line verification of every finding marked CONFIRMED below. No runtime traces were run. Items marked INFERRED rest on code reading only.\n\nHeadline: dap is designed as a gated service, with membership grants as the hard gate. At the HTTP layer the hosted scope Worker behaves as a public one, because a valid signature is self-certification (any fresh keypair passes), so every \"signature only\" gate is pre-authentication in the method's sense.\n\n== 1. Early reachability: work done and state written before the grant check ==\n\n1.1 Scope creation is open to any keypair. POST /v1/scopes lets any key `install` a register or `found` a directory. A genesis whose proof holds is written even when its act is refused (packages/derive/src/genesis.ts:93). The register's install rule \"checks no more\" than the seed (packages/platform/src/register.ts:278). docs/scopes.md line 57 states nothing checks installation authority. The host pin (ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope) blocks repository creation only; a full room tree with membership, rules and destination can be built, that membership issues read sessions under the deployment secret, and it can register hosted MCP agents. No per-key, per-address or count bound applies; only join/enrol have serving limits (packages/scope/src/limits.ts). CONFIRMED.\n\n1.2 Any well-formed scope ID instantiates a persistent Durable Object before any check. The constructor runs about twenty CREATE TABLE/INDEX/TRIGGER statements (packages/scope/src/sqlite.ts:82-141; also local-signers.ts, operator.ts, request-index.ts, sessions.ts:405). Reached by every GET/POST under /v1/scopes/:id (worker.ts:166-168), /site/:id (site/host.ts:126), /applications/:id (applications/route.ts:50, before the trust check at :56), the hosted MCP registry for any membership ID (worker.ts:603; hosted.ts:198), and every foreign fact an outside signer names in an act, up to usesPerEntry 128 (namespace.ts:272-297; core.ts:494-498). CONFIRMED.\n\n1.3 Turn order (core.ts:557-655): signature (core.ts:565) -\u003e parse -\u003e receiver reads -\u003e foreign fetches (core.ts:591) -\u003e authority observation (core.ts:599) -\u003e timed drain, which writes timed entries (turn.ts:234) -\u003e rule walk and rule-expression evaluation -\u003e commit where check 9 refuses `unauthorized` (judge.ts:327-344). A random key can trigger foreign fetches and the drain. Rule-expression evaluation is correctly after check 9 (judge.ts:372-379). The per-run `kept` observation map has no cap (authority.ts:115,252). CONFIRMED.\n\n1.4 Public /site reads mint an Artifacts read token per request and attempt a revoke afterwards, with no session and no limit (site/host.ts:181-205; site/route.ts:44). CONFIRMED.\n\n1.5 Hosted MCP control routes create the registry object for any membership ID and run an `#expire` write before the control signature is verified (worker.ts:599-604; hosted.ts:486, 167-175). Body digest is computed after the signature check (good). Control routes have no rate limit. The bearer path reads no JSON-RPC body before the bearer passes (good). CONFIRMED.\n\n1.6 Signed reads by any non-local key start a full history chain walk before refusal (object.ts:598-617; signed-reads.ts:267-323). INFERRED cost; path CONFIRMED.\n\n== 2. Default configuration: reachable by default, not needed by the default deployment ==\n\n2.1 The hosted MCP endpoint is bound on every room Worker (apps/room/wrangler.jsonc REGISTRIES/AGENTS). Its default tool list includes `create`, `install_application`, `credential`, `prepare`, `join` and raw reads `record`, `step`, `text` (service.ts:562-597). Tools hidden for lack of a grant remain callable by name (service.ts:353-357). CONFIRMED.\n\n2.2 Every shipped platform version is creatable for new scopes (core.ts:446-451; platform/src/index.ts:241-243), and the defaults are old: register@3, directory@3, membership@2, rules@2 (index.ts:229). Membership before @6 uses bearer-secret invitations, not key-bound proofs; rules@1-2 do not check rule text at activate. CONFIRMED.\n\n2.3 Dormant but linked: the GitHub port (worker.ts:90,427), the ScopeService entrypoint with no binding (worker.ts:522), the demo creation route with hard-coded workers.dev origins (packages/scope/src/demo-creation.ts:8). The fixture archive driver is correctly not wired. Artifacts binding, R2 bucket, metrics and 100% console logs are bound regardless of configuration. CONFIRMED.\n\n2.4 Token lifetimes. Any active member can mint 24-hour read tokens (`destination.read-token` is in every role, no guards, destination.ts:516-528) with no count or rate limit. An unread token's plaintext is never swept (credential-store.ts:172-212). A hosted agent's bearer never expires (hosted.ts:531-549); its plaintext sits in stored control answers for seven days past notAfter (hosted.ts:50,250,462-471). CONFIRMED.\n\n2.5 The route table in the worker.ts header omits four served routes (query-items, application-projection, requests, reservation-snapshot), and the deployed entry is apps/room/fetch.ts, not worker.ts's default export. CONFIRMED.\n\n== 3. Configuration interaction: pairs that silently weaken a control ==\n\n3.1 Same-origin application screens + page secret in localStorage. The room page keeps the member's signing secret in localStorage (apps/room/page/src/main.ts:64-83). Trusted package assets are served from the same origin under script-src 'self' (applications/route.ts:1-3,19). The code states \"Same-origin delivery is not an isolation boundary.\" Any trusted publisher's script can read the secret. The inguz.space sandbox origin is the designed fix and is not deployed. CONFIRMED.\n\n3.2 Extents. `approvals: 0` is accepted for every extent except `rules` (extents.ts:77-78,121). `approver` may be any action name, including one every role holds (extents.ts:109,122,490). A mistyped pattern falls to the catch-all (extents.ts:338-340). No warning at validation or activate. CONFIRMED.\n\n3.3 `ownerMayReview` defaults true in rules@4, which the demo cohort pins; the controller-review check is then skipped on every extent except `rules` (rules-scope.ts:684-697; extents.ts:491). CONFIRMED.\n\n3.4 When extents exist the destination ignores a check marked `required` (reservation.ts:267-286); the lane enforces it from its own copy of the rules, refreshed only by rules-wanted (lanes/src/change.ts:1290-1328). Code CONFIRMED; staleness INFERRED.\n\n3.5 Health vs. wiring. /health reads only registerScope; the Artifacts wiring also requires the namespace match. A namespace mismatch leaves wiring at NO_OUTSIDE while health answers 200 (health.ts:60-65; artifacts-wiring.ts:24,88). One malformed optional GitHub secret turns the whole GitHub wiring off with health still 200 (github-wiring.ts:51-73). Both configs set to different registers: health 503 \"ambiguous\" while both hosts still serve (worker.ts:425-429). The site route uses a looser config parser than the wiring (site/host.ts:145-153 vs artifacts-wiring.ts:41-46). CONFIRMED.\n\n3.6 DEPLOYMENT is parsed in five places with different bounds: sessions 1-128 bytes (sessions.ts:101), demo up to 256 (demo-creation.ts:22), health, metrics (no bound), screens. A name of 129-256 bytes turns sessions off and leaves demo authority on. CONFIRMED.\n\n3.7 MCP `install_application` fetches the Git blob from any HTTPS host before any trust check; a trust row holds no URI (service.ts:966-977; admission.ts:30). Only a bearer and a configured application room are needed. CONFIRMED.\n\n3.8 APPLICATION_TRUST revoked after an install: screens answer 404, installed definitions keep judging acts (worker.ts:432; applications/route.ts:49,55). CONFIRMED.\n\n3.9 Join limits are keyed by CF-Connecting-IP (worker.ts:320); hosted agents' in-process calls (worker.ts:682) and service-binding callers have no address and are never counted. Null address CONFIRMED; agent path INFERRED.\n\n3.10 `npm run deploy:scope` has no --keep-vars (package.json:20); settings set outside the file are dropped on deploy and fail closed, visible only as 503s (docs/deploy.md:128-130). CONFIRMED.\n\n3.11 A directory with no creator made by `found` directly on POST /v1/scopes runs no founding-policy rule (genesis.ts:191-198). Host authority excludes such directories (host-wiring.ts:20-36). Path CONFIRMED; impact INFERRED (storage and compute only).\n\n3.12 Founding policy `open` silently ignores a `founders` list (register.ts:293-300). CONFIRMED.\n\n3.13 dap-grow and artroom-scope share the artroom-demo Artifacts namespace, the content bucket and the metrics dataset; only code pins keep them apart. INFERRED.\n\n== 4. What is already right (keep) ==\n\nNo HTTP route accepts a delivery; delivery is namespace RPC only. Rule expressions run only after check 9, under the restricted@1 profile with pure functions and budgets. Session MAC compared in constant time before parsing. Credential-in-URL refused first. The P2 from the 2026-10-13 MCP review (join accepts any service URL) is landed (b4adc8cb). APPLICATION_TRUST unset or malformed fails closed. SESSION_SECRET/DEPLOYMENT missing fails closed. Credential reads are bound to the signing key of the read-token act. Hosted MCP body digest after signature, no body read before bearer.\n\n== 5. Remediation to file (builder, with checker review), in the method's reduction patterns ==\n\nR1 Public to gated: on a deployed Worker, refuse POST /v1/scopes creation unless it is the pinned register's install or a `found` judged by that register (or an explicit deployment setting that opens it). Closes 1.1, 3.11, 3.12.\nR2 No object before proof: check scope existence cheaply before idFromName (an index of known scope IDs), or defer table creation to the genesis write. Closes 1.2 and the registry half of 1.5.\nR3 Reorder the turn: for acts whose authority observation already fails, refuse before foreign fetches and before the timed drain. Cap the `kept` map. Closes 1.3.\nR4 Site reads: cache or pool read tokens per repository and ref; rate-limit site reads by address. Closes 1.4.\nR5 Hosted MCP: opt-in per deployment (setting or separate Worker); narrow default tool mode with `create` and `install_application` off unless configured; bearer expiry; stored answers without the bearer plaintext; a bound on #failures. Closes 2.1, 2.4 (bearer), 1.5 (expire write after signature).\nR6 Versions: creation accepts only the newest cohort plus versions already pinned by live scopes; raise NEWEST defaults (membership@8, rules@10, directory@16). Closes 2.2.\nR7 Extents at activate: refuse approvals below 1 outside an explicit opt-in field, restrict approver to review actions, refuse patterns that match no path, make ownerMayReview explicit (no default) in the next rules version. Closes 3.2, 3.3.\nR8 Deploy the inguz.space sandbox shim and serve application screens from it; move the page's signing secret out of localStorage (non-extractable key in IndexedDB as the Counter does, or PRF-derived unlock). Closes 3.1.\nR9 One parser per setting; /health reports wiring state (NO_OUTSIDE), not only registerScope; one DEPLOYMENT bound; add --keep-vars to deploy:scope or a plan check. Closes 3.5, 3.6, 3.10.\nR10 install_application: check the release against APPLICATION_TRUST (or a declared host allowlist) before the fetch; trust rows carry a host. Closes 3.7.\nR11 Trust revocation: when a release leaves APPLICATION_TRUST, refuse acts under its definitions (or record the revocation as an act). Closes 3.8.\nR12 Limits: a per-key and per-address window for creation and signed reads, like JoinLimits; count in-process and service-binding joins by key when no address exists. Closes 1.6, 3.9.\nR13 Token hygiene: a sweep of unread read tokens at their end; a per-member count of open read tokens. Closes 2.4.\nR14 Usage against configuration: a query over 30 days of METRICS route points (place, answer) listing routes and platform versions never used; retire what the query shows. Closes 2.3.\n\n== 6. Documentation and threat model (agreed direction: do these) ==\n\nD1 Entry-point inventory with gates, one table per Worker (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending, dap-grow-simulator, dap-home): route, gate class (none / self-signed / membership / session / admin / bearer / control), pre-gate work, state written, bounds, outbound calls. Backed by a test that enumerates routes and asserts each gate class so the table cannot drift. Fix the worker.ts header table or replace it with this.\nD2 The scope contract and the authority note onto main. The two normative documents that about 400 code comments cite by section number are not on main: latest copies are notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md on refs/heads/request/scope-contract-r15 and notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md (revision 28 at 8b1c3c9d) on refs/heads/request/authority-r20. Either land them under notes/ (or docs/) with their section numbers, or renumber docs/scopes.md and rewrite the citations. Add a script that checks every \"(section N)\" citation resolves.\nD3 Settings reference: every env var and binding, where it is read, its parser, its failure mode (closed / open / inconsistent) and what /health reports for it.\nD4 Trust-boundary page per deployment: what the session secret, the Artifacts binding, the R2 bucket and the MCP namespaces protect, and which Workers share them.\nD5 Definition-author security page: what validation refuses versus allows (zero guards, approvals 0, any-action approver, vacuous guard forms: count min 0, each over empty, ifPresent absent, notIn with no signer, fact with empty where), with the fail-open list.\nD6 A short threat model as invariants with named witness tests, in the style of docs/testing.md: \"no act takes effect without an observed grant\", \"no outside call without a sealed entry\", \"a session reads only its own membership's scopes\", \"no object exists without a verified genesis\", \"no credential leaves custody except to the key that asked\". D1 and D3 are its evidence tables. A SECURITY.md pointing at D1-D6, the reviews, and a reporting path. The only in-tree security review (notes/reviews/2026-10-04-security-review.md) covers the parked model.\n\n== 7. Instruction to planner ==\n\nFile remediation requests to builder for R1-R14 and D1-D6, grouped sensibly (suggested: R1+R2+R3+R12 as one creation-and-admission head; R4+R13 tokens; R5 hosted MCP; R6+R7 versions and extents; R8 sandbox; R9+R10+R11 settings and trust; R14 usage query; D1+D2 first, then D3-D6), each with acceptance conditions that name the finding it closes and a witness test, and with checker review on every head. Order: D1 and D2 first (they make every later review cheaper), then R1-R3 and R8 (largest reductions), then the rest. Keep the hosted service deployable after each head; nothing here should wait for the demo-room archive slice unless the planner judges a conflict. Reply with an assert resting on this request that lists the filed request IDs, their grouping and their order.","body":{"conditions":"1. Remediation requests filed to builder covering R1-R14 and D1-D6 below, grouped as suggested in section 7 or better, each with acceptance conditions that name the finding(s) it closes and a witness test, and with checker review required on every head. 2. Order: D1 and D2 first, then R1-R3 and R8, then the rest. 3. An assert resting on this request that lists the filed request IDs, their grouping and their order, so Hugh can follow them. 4. The hosted service stays deployable after each head. Direction from Hugh on 2026-10-21: the documentation and threat-model items D1-D6 are agreed and are to be done.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}